INSERT INTO feature VALUES('filler-generator','identity','The filler generator (fill[n, k])','unbiased-composition','partial','unique','dependent provers','`fill[n, k](chain(m), t, d)` lifts a cell `t` over a chain of paths along the entries it takes as paths one layer deeper, the set `X`, at a stratum the chain sub-site certifies. `d` lists the chain''s cells, or its whole pasting context in Catt''s order. `t` is a function of those entries into a path, between two composites of the cells or between the chain''s two ends. The node''s type is the square from `Path.step(t[X⁻], v ↑ X)` to `Path.step(u ↑ X, t[X⁺])`, each lift a whisker along the composites. Based path induction proves it, each vertex path of `X` first and then each cell of `X`, and the kernel replays the proof. A decided fill computes to its induction wherever it stands, in a type as in a term, so a filler over a `Path.here` cell reduces to `Path.here` and `Path.walk` over it to its base. Examples 1.1 to 1.3 of Benjamin et al. 2025 check at the types Catt answers, Example 1.3 at the associator over all three cells. At level two, `fill[n, k](chain(m, (a₁, …, aₘ)), t, cells)` names `X` by its columns, a column of one 2-cell for each cell of `X`, and level two certifies the shape. Over a level-two shape''s pasting context, its points fixed, each column is a chain one level up, and `t`''s sides compose the columns'' first 1-cells and their last. Example 1.4 checks at constant verticals. The fill reads its shape as `compose` does, one Batanin tree at the level of its cells. A stratum the chains do not certify, a square the generator does not make, a set that is no pasting context, columns that are not the cells of `X`, a tree past level two and a `Flow` or bridge cell are refused by name. The printer and the formatter write the form back as it is written. `natassoc` fills the associator over the 3-chain beside `assoc_nat`, and the two agree at a `Path.here` cell. Their agreement at a general cell, the composites at dimension 3 at Catt''s types with free verticals, and the `Flow` and bridge instances are owed.','core-term core-checker core-nbe surface-lowering surface-pretty surface-format','corpus/ledger/diagnostics/FillUncertified.gandr corpus/ledger/diagnostics/NoFiller.gandr corpus/ledger/diagnostics/GeneratorFamilyUnsupported.gandr corpus/ledger/features/naturality.gandr corpus/model/identity/walk-over-fillers.gandr','corpus/ledger/features/filler-generator.gandr','#4120 #3833 #4093 #642');
